---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About Blanc Browser — Independent by design"
  description="Blanc is a minimal desktop browser built on Chromium, with a floating Island, built-in ad and tracker blocking, and no advertising business."
  path="/about"
  page="about"
  current="about"
  ogTitle="About Blanc Browser — Independent by design"
  ogDescription="What Blanc is, what it stands for, and how it is built and funded."
>
<main id="main-content" class="about-page">
  <section class="about-hero" aria-labelledby="about-title">
    <p class="section-kicker">about blanc</p>
    <h1 id="about-title">Independent by design.</h1>
    <p>Blanc is a desktop browser for macOS, Windows and Linux, built on Chromium. One floating Island holds your tabs, navigation and page controls, so the page stays in front, and ad and tracker blocking is built in.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="about-proof-list" aria-label="What Blanc stands for and how it is built">
    <article class="about-proof-row">
      <p class="about-label">the idea</p>
      <div>
        <h2>Less browser around the page.</h2>
        <p>Tabs, navigation and page controls share a compact Island in a slim top band. Its expanded panel opens over the page.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/island">Meet the Island <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="about-proof-row">
      <p class="about-label">built in</p>
      <div>
        <h2>Blocking that is already there.</h2>
        <p>Blanc Blocker stops ads and known trackers at the browser level, without asking you to start with an extension. It is on by default and also protects private tabs.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/features/ad-blocking">See site controls <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="about-proof-row">
      <p class="about-label">the model</p>
      <div>
        <h2>Independently controlled, without an ads business.</h2>
        <p>Blanc has no venture funding and no investors setting its product agenda or exit timetable. It is not funded by selling ads or turning browsing activity into an audience product. That keeps the incentives simple: make a browser people want to keep using.</p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="about-proof-row">
      <p class="about-label">open source</p>
      <div>
        <h2>Code you can read.</h2>
        <p>Blanc’s own code is MIT-licensed and public on GitHub. Its name and logos, and the third-party components it includes, keep their own terms.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/support#open-source">Licensing and exceptions <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="about-proof-row">
      <p class="about-label">the evidence</p>
      <div>
        <h2>Public checks, with their limits stated.</h2>
        <p>Blanc publishes source, release checks, signed manifests, an SBOM, and compatibility evidence. No independent external security audit has been completed. Those records support specific claims; they are not an external certification or a blanket security guarantee.</p>
        <p>Blanc has no general third-party extension runtime. Its optional 1Password bridge and device-bound Touch ID passkeys are macOS-only.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/trust">Privacy and security <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="about-proof-row about-supporter">
      <p class="about-label">how it’s funded</p>
      <div>
        <h2>The browser is complete without a subscription.</h2>
        <p>Browsing essentials and ordinary tab groups are free. Blanc Patron is the optional subscription: US$30 per year or US$4 per month, plus applicable tax. It adds saved Named Workspaces. Creating a named workspace requires an active Patron subscription. If membership lapses, existing workspaces remain openable, switchable, and automatically updated. Renaming and removing existing workspaces continue to work if it lapses. Earlier one-time supporters keep their lifetime Patron access.</p>
        <a class="text-link" data-track="supporter_click" data-cta-position="about-supporter" href="https://buy.polar.sh/polar_cl_auwRq39Q2hIVLJwANEqFWgWuZ8DGjdJmEI4mE0JaNDf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">become a Patron <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <p class="about-maker">Made by <a href="https://bnfy.me" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Bananify</a>, an independent software studio. AI assists implementation and security review; the maintainer remains accountable for product decisions and release approval. AI-assisted checks and maintainer review do not constitute an independent security audit.</p>

  <section class="about-close" aria-labelledby="about-close-title">
    <p class="section-kicker">support is human</p>
    <h2 id="about-close-title">Questions reach a human.</h2>
    <p>Email <!--email_off--><a href="mailto:support@blancbrowser.com">support@blancbrowser.com</a><!--/email_off-->, or see the <a href="/changelog" data-track="feature_cta_click" data-feature="changelog" data-cta-position="about-close">public changelog</a> for what shipped most recently.</p>
  </section>
</main>
</BaseLayout>
